From d810de4f09efec79dc44fe924646935762a16192 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: auditor <audit@local>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 00:26:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] statistics: hypothesis registry + Deflated Sharpe - the
 multiple-testing layer

INVARIANT PROTECTED: a result must survive the search width that produced
it. This is the layer the programme never had, and its absence is the most
likely explanation for the entire forward record.

THE HOLE. Eleven families are frozen ABSENT; one cleared a 95th-percentile
bar. There is no multiple-testing correction anywhere in the tree
(grepped: deflated sharpe / multiple.?testing / bonferroni / family.?wise /
n_trials / false discovery - zero hits outside tests).

project_status.py:282 applies exactly the right reasoning at width THREE:
"best-of-three at a 95th percentile occurs about 14% of the time under a
global null". Confirmed: 1 - 0.95**3 = 0.1426. That reasoning is never
applied at the width the programme actually searched.

CORRECTED COUNT - the collaborating audit said width 11 / 43%. It is
width TWELVE / 46.0%. signals/ holds 10 modules, but
project_status.FROZEN_ABSENT records ELEVEN frozen families: it includes
`technical_analysis` and `closed_analyser`, measured and frozen without a
surviving module. 11 frozen + 1 cleared = 12 trials. Seeding the registry
from the directory listing would have UNDERCOUNTED by two and produced a
weaker correction than the evidence supports, so the seed reads
project_status, and a test pins that it does.

Under a global null in which NO family has edge, the chance that at least
one of twelve clears a 95% bar is 46.0%. funding_carry_fade_btc_v1 cleared
at that width and then lost money forward (n=2, mean net R -0.8358).
Selection under a global null is the most parsimonious account of that
sequence, and until now the programme could not state it numerically
because nothing counted the trials.

WHAT IS ADDED (no gate reads any of it; nothing is re-scored):
  tools/deflated_sharpe.py
    family_wise_false_positive_rate   1-(1-a)**n  (reproduces the tree's
                                      own 14% at width 3 - test pins it)
    expected_max_sharpe_under_null    Bailey & Lopez de Prado 2014 eq.5.
                                      VALIDATED against Monte Carlo at
                                      widths 3/12/50: within 1%.
    deflated_sharpe_ratio             P(true Sharpe>0) after correcting for
                                      trials, skew, kurtosis, sample length.
    minimum_track_record_length       could a sample this small EVER support
                                      the claim (ask before waiting a year).
    effective_n_trials                correlation-adjusted count. NOT the
                                      default: 12 families over one price
                                      path are not independent, so the raw
                                      count over-corrects, which is the safe
                                      direction. Using the looser number
                                      requires a written justification.
  tools/hypothesis_registry.py        append-only census, seeded
                                      retroactively, refuses overwrites.

A BUG I FOUND IN MY OWN IMPLEMENTATION, kept visible because it is the
instructive part: `sr` is a PER-OBSERVATION Sharpe while the order
statistic is z-scale. Subtracting them directly (sharpe_variance=1.0, the
naive reading of the paper) compares ~0.3 against a bar of ~1.66 and
returns dsr = 0 for EVERY input - an instrument that looks like rigour and
discriminates nothing. The default now scales the bar by 1/sqrt(n-1), and
test_units_are_consistent_between_sharpe_and_the_null_bar is a regression
guard. Post-fix the estimator behaves: pure noise 0.15, real signal 0.70,
same signal with one fat-tailed loss 0.29.

HONEST LIMITS, stated in the module: trials are not independent (raw count
over-corrects, deliberately); a registry starting today cannot recover
trials nobody recorded, so 12 is a FLOOR and the true correction is
harsher; passing DSR does not make a strategy profitable, it removes one
specific way of being fooled.

NOT DONE: Combinatorial Purged CV (the third leg). HORIZON=5 and LOCKUP=1
are the right purge/embargo parameters; replacing the single pre-declared
OOS cut is a larger change that must not be made in the same patch as the
counter, because a new CV scheme applied to an already-seen window is
itself a new trial.

Tests: tests/test_multiple_testing.py, 26 tests. Full suite 5,039 passed.
